moin (1.10.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New version number 1.10.0 for the Python 3 port of MoinMoin 1.9.11
    (the static files are now served under /moin_static1100).
  * XML-RPC v2 sends strings as <string> again (not as base64).
  * moin-mkwiki: with -s the superuser also gets all ACL rights.
  * The compiled page cache is tied to the Python version that wrote it.
  * The Python 3 port and this packaging were made with the assistance of
    Claude (Anthropic AI); the files written or modified by Claude are
    marked with a comment at their top.

 -- Gabriele 'asbesto' Zaverio <aladarmrgradymezil@gmail.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0200

moin (1.9.11+py3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * MoinMoin 1.9.11 ported to Python 3 (tested with Python 3.13).
    - Wiki data (pages, users, edit-log, attachments) stay compatible
      with MoinMoin 1.9.x on Python 2, in both directions.
    - Uses the system pygments, passlib and parsedatetime; ships
      werkzeug 1.0.1, flup 1.0.3 and secure_cookie (needed versions).
  * Works without systemd: optional sysvinit script for standalone
    wiki servers; WSGI (Apache mod_wsgi, uWSGI, gunicorn), CGI,
    FastCGI and SCGI are supported, too.
  * moin-mkwiki creates new wiki instances; with -s the superuser also
    gets all ACL rights (acl_rights_before).

 -- Gabriele 'asbesto' Zaverio <aladarmrgradymezil@gmail.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0200
